{#
  One post, in the Paper design (doc-9): `article.blog-post.h-entry` opening on
  a kicker that names its kind (Article, Note, Reply) and the categories it is
  filed under.

  An article, and a reply with a title, has the only headline: the title as its
  `p-name` and the author's `description` under it as the deck, a
  `p-summary`. A post with no title opens on its words, set larger. A reply
  cites what it answers above its words, or above its header when it has one.
  Then the Published line, the tags, a rule and the bio. The neighbouring posts,
  the conversation and the comment form follow the entry.

  The Published line is inside the `e-content` on purpose. It is what the
  source design does, and it is what makes a reader who copies the words out
  take the date and the permalink with them.
#}
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}
{% import "partials/tags.njk" as taxonomy with context %}
{% import "partials/kicker.njk" as kicker with context %}
{% import "partials/lang.njk" as language with context %}

{#- Who the bio credits: the person the file names, and otherwise whoever the
    site is by, which is what the source theme's bio reads. A post naming
    nobody on a site whose author setting names nobody either has no bio at
    all. It is set out here rather than in the block because
    `layouts/base.njk` reads it too — a page with a bio carries the site menu
    in it, and the page footer prints the menu only where there is none. -#}
{% set bioAuthor = author or siteAuthor %}

{% block content %}
{% set entryUrl = page.url or url %}
<article class="blog-post h-entry"{{ language.attr(lang) }}>
  {#- A post with no name of its own (a note, or a reply without a title) is
      its words, so it opens on them in sight. Its page still needs one h1 to
      navigate by, so it gets one that says what it is, who wrote it and when,
      hidden from sight. It is no `p-name`: a parser would take that as a
      title and read the note as an article. -#}
  {% if named %}
  {#- A reply cites the post it answers, whose URL is also the link its
      webmention points a receiver at. -#}
  {% include "partials/reply-context.njk" %}
  <header class="post-header">
    {{ kicker.line(postType | capitalize, false, false, categories) }}
    <h1 class="p-name">{{ title }}</h1>
    {% if description %}
    <p class="post-deck p-summary">{{ description }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </header>
  {% else %}
  <h1 class="screen-reader-text">
    {{- "Reply" if postType == "reply" else "Note" }}
    {%- if bioAuthor.name %} by {{ bioAuthor.name }}{% endif %}
    {%- if date %}, {{ date | date("readable", none, lang) }}{% endif -%}
  </h1>
  {{ kicker.line(postType | capitalize, false, false, categories) }}
  {% include "partials/reply-context.njk" %}
  {% endif %}

  <section class="e-content">
    {{ content | safe }}
    <p class="entry-meta">
      {#- A post tagged `indienews` opens the line with the link that submits
          it there, which is how IndieNews is told the post is for it. -#}
      {%- if "indienews" in tags %}
      <a class="u-category small" href="https://news.indieweb.org/en">#indienews</a>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if date %}
      <a href="{{ entryUrl | url }}" class="u-url"><time class="small dt-published" datetime="{{ date | date("iso") }}">Published {{ date | date("readable", none, lang) }}</time></a>
      {%- endif %}
      {#- Updated only when it is a different day in the site's own timezone:
          a typo fixed an hour after publishing is not news. -#}
      {%- if updated and (not date or (updated | date("html")) != (date | date("html"))) %}
      {% if date %}<span aria-hidden="true">·</span> {% endif %}<time class="small dt-updated" datetime="{{ updated | date("iso") }}">Updated {{ updated | date("readable", none, lang) }}</time>
      {%- endif -%}
    </p>
  </section>

  {# The tags, inside the entry so that each link is a `p-category` of it. The
     categories are in the kicker. #}
  {{ taxonomy.list(tags) }}
  {#- The rule and the footer are the bio's own: a post nobody is credited with
      ends at its words rather than at an empty box. -#}
  {% if bioAuthor %}
  <hr>
  <footer>
    {% include "partials/bio.njk" %}
  </footer>
  {% endif %}
</article>

{# The post either side of this one, as two cards. Each is on the context only
   when there is one, so the ends of the archive draw one card and a site of a
   single post draws none. #}
{% if previous or next %}
<nav class="blog-post-nav" aria-label="Neighbouring posts">
  <ul>
    {% if previous %}
    <li><a rel="prev" href="{{ previous.url | url }}"><span class="blog-post-nav-label">Previous</span> {{ previous.title }}</a></li>
    {% endif %}
    {% if next %}
    <li><a rel="next" href="{{ next.url | url }}"><span class="blog-post-nav-label">Next</span> {{ next.title }}</a></li>
    {% endif %}
  </ul>
</nav>
{% endif %}

{# Only a post that has been replied to, liked or boosted has one of these. #}
{% if conversation %}
{% include "partials/conversation.njk" %}
{% endif %}

{# And only one that is still taking comments has a form (TASK-50). #}
{% if commentForm %}
{% include "partials/comment-form.njk" %}
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
